<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:07:43Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>UK: 5 arrested after 'major incident' near Fairford air base</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45fa282ee661d1e06959ac4ed0bad49196b2c2e1efd7cfd021e1e896c8c69ee4</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:07:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T13:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-5-arrested-after-major-incident-near-fairford-air-base/a-79447992--072dcc5d3fc3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-5-arrested-after-major-incident-near-fairford-air-base/a-79447992?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Scores of homes were evacuated in the UK town of Whelford, near an air base used by the US military, with bomb disposal teams checking "suspicious vehicles" at the scene. Police said five men had been arrested.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>European cities seek ways of boosting affordable housing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:87fcfcd9657f7d172441312cab63125c7892812156eb70eec8c8c1a4b1667e69</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:07:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T13:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/european-cities-seek-ways-of-boosting-affordable-housing/a-79438939--fc67dbf8271c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/european-cities-seek-ways-of-boosting-affordable-housing/a-79438939?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In many major urban centers of Europe, the housing shortage has become an explosive social issue. DW looks into various models that have been put in place across the continent.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Switzerland: Voters reject stricter view of neutrality</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:243029d273a0bc70489dc2d0afca346e45afe8b303192220d25ee8ab53077dcf</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:07:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/switzerland-voters-reject-stricter-view-of-neutrality/a-79446996--5986041c2b6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/switzerland-voters-reject-stricter-view-of-neutrality/a-79446996?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Early projections show Swiss voters rejecting a stricter application of the country's vaunted neutrality. Swiss neutrality has been enshrined in the constitution since 1848.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pope decries 'scourge' of sexual abuse during France visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:932271c194230fd39441bc35f6bdc027fa1bbf66015a58f40efd2ff8498b657e</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:07:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T11:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-decries-scourge-of-sexual-abuse-during-france-visit/a-79449335--995ba7f8239c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-decries-scourge-of-sexual-abuse-during-france-visit/a-79449335?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French bishops took "courageous" steps when faced with "the painful scourge of abuse of minors," Pope Leo XIV told the high-ranking clerics before his scheduled meeting with survivors at the Catholic shrine of Lourdes.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Are Germans giving up their beloved meat and sausages?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1aae9e5f07fd83e167b69f62e98a0b25a6dadbf26a3995c899b076aa23ed26f</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:07:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T10:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-are-germans-giving-up-their-beloved-meat-and-sausages/live-79441034--d9fb5f1aa888.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-are-germans-giving-up-their-beloved-meat-and-sausages/live-79441034?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germans used to be all about sausages and meat. While those do remain popular, things seem to be slowly changing. There also are new insights into the economic side of East Germany's espionage DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Northern Ireland: Pro-UK march to go through Catholic area</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a28fb42713604eb949ba0d5b3b2493298ae6b73f952960b07ebad50584bb6a0</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:07:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T09:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/northern-ireland-pro-uk-march-to-go-through-catholic-area/a-79447441--5aa601872486.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/northern-ireland-pro-uk-march-to-go-through-catholic-area/a-79447441?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It's the first time the march has been allowed to go through the area since 1997. Overnight, a court ruling allowed it to take place after a series of last-minute legal challenges that reached Belfast's High Court.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Kolkata's SRFTI students allege violent attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dce8adffb6d5c90fd3c49ec7103088f693bf3eacad591ca13d4a21e0f774a445</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T08:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-kolkata-s-srfti-students-allege-violent-attack/live-79440869--92d965222a7c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-kolkata-s-srfti-students-allege-violent-attack/live-79440869?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Students at Kolkata's Satyajit Ray Film and Television Institute say they were attacked with knives after confronting an outside group over a meeting they allege was affiliated with the right-wing Hindu RSS. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran sticks to Hormuz plan after Trump rejects it</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ccc6feddf4e3e746ed338a113488fa6b25875b545108f11657aa06bb240e0841</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:07:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-sticks-to-hormuz-plan-after-trump-rejects-it/a-79447432--8e8b9e348264.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-sticks-to-hormuz-plan-after-trump-rejects-it/a-79447432?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iranian officials that while they were aware of Trump's comments on rejecting the new proposal, they had not received a formal message rejecting the plan that would open the Strait of Hormuz.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>No public mentions of Taiwan at official Xi and Trump meeting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a81d407ff18138ab74a7579aa95724294095a6d734a64135fe002205d4d6ed57</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:07:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T08:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/no-public-mentions-of-taiwan-at-official-xi-and-trump-meeting/a-79445378--29352cbff0b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/no-public-mentions-of-taiwan-at-official-xi-and-trump-meeting/a-79445378?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At a high-profile summit between Presidents Donald Trump and Xi Jinping in Washington, there was much talk of trade and artificial intelligence. One of the most contentious issues, Taiwan, was only discussed in private.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China sends two giant pandas off to Atlanta zoo after Xi-Trump summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e9441e8384c31eb83da11e897c5c31206f9c9a056ee0dd237c2dbeb33c7236c</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:07:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T07:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-sends-two-giant-pandas-off-to-atlanta-zoo-after-xi-trump-summit/a-79447128--ab8e1682ffd9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-sends-two-giant-pandas-off-to-atlanta-zoo-after-xi-trump-summit/a-79447128?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ping Ping and Fu Shuang took off to Atlanta on a FedEx plane, with steamed corn buns, carrots and bamboo to snack on during the flight. Their trip is one of the few concrete things to come out the Xi-Trump summit.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Gunmen kill 27 people in two mass shootings in South Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc5b723d67441a2d0e84a7305e1f4eca76e693c6dad6d593b0e457f1df4dbc48</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:07:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T06:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gunmen-kill-27-people-in-two-mass-shootings-in-south-africa/a-79447130--f3bd024a1578.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gunmen-kill-27-people-in-two-mass-shootings-in-south-africa/a-79447130?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South African police have launched a search for suspects after 17 people were found dead at a tavern southwest of Johannesburg. A separate tavern shooting near Cape Town left 10 dead.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why farmers are pairing crops with solar panels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc55fd6d221118fc60a690ffb9aa0dbbe0351a4ee4fb78cacbf68081428912a8</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:07:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T04:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-farmers-are-pairing-crops-with-solar-panels/a-79233970--008efaae1ed6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-farmers-are-pairing-crops-with-solar-panels/a-79233970?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From cooler soil to paid grazing land, farmers in the US are finding that solar panels can do more than generate power.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Powerful storm batters northeast US, hundreds of flights canceled</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:213a44c8b6d738f7b9e0a9f91158f93cbede45365d7e60c3ee4bdbf9d6f766e8</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:06:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T03:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/powerful-storm-batters-northeast-us-hundreds-of-flights-canceled/a-79446676--6ec8e25a25ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/powerful-storm-batters-northeast-us-hundreds-of-flights-canceled/a-79446676?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of flights were canceled and thousands were delayed as a nor'easter brought flooding, power cuts and travel disruption to cities like New York, Boston and Philadelphia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spain: Thousands protest in Madrid against housing crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:738264de6c0c9c037929c64e434384dcb3fb06d0969d2963ff4bbb8c4b8e88b3</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:06:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T01:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-thousands-protest-in-madrid-against-housing-crisis/a-79446662--133b5faee12d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-thousands-protest-in-madrid-against-housing-crisis/a-79446662?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands rallied in the Spanish capital after an 87-year-old woman was dramatically evicted from her home this week. Protesters called for measures to curb rising costs and reduce evictions.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Backlash over data centers tests Europe's AI ambitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e685f3c48548164b20286e359f17eea48065503633af28be8805f0e0d8e2bdbd</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:06:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T18:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/backlash-over-data-centers-tests-europe-s-ai-ambitions/a-79419800--224361aa983d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/backlash-over-data-centers-tests-europe-s-ai-ambitions/a-79419800?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Massive data centers needed to run AI are triggering protests across Europe. Their operators counter that they boost digital sovereignty and energy independence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China, US agree to set up channel for AI safety incidents</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8201862ea874e2f4b1d9f256df231f8db32e3d38e683a2bb4a5f84feccfd89b4</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:06:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T16:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-us-agree-to-set-up-channel-for-ai-safety-incidents/a-79443351--116e0ce66bfc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-us-agree-to-set-up-channel-for-ai-safety-incidents/a-79443351?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following the summit between US President Donald Trump and Chinese President Xi Jinping, the two superpowers pledged to set up a "communication channel" for AI incidents and boost coordination on military matters.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump rejects Iran proposal to reopen Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:377fe6ea9ec4e60cb4e5e4aaccf03e96f1c3de8fc8692fdb1e82e16b6846fc68</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:06:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T16:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-rejects-iran-proposal-to-reopen-strait-of-hormuz/a-79444893--025adfe63f1d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-rejects-iran-proposal-to-reopen-strait-of-hormuz/a-79444893?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump says he has rejected an Iranian proposal to reopen the Strait of Hormuz and put an end to hostilities. "I'd like to make a deal, too," he said. "But that deal would not be acceptable."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Paris: Pope Leo XIV celebrates Mass before huge crowd</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79ba897ee50e7b3f0c6f44cd81d359aaafb5afd29e4761e6ff6853b07fe0cfe8</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:06:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T16:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/paris-pope-leo-xiv-celebrates-mass-before-huge-crowd/a-79442864--ce9a98bc1a48.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/paris-pope-leo-xiv-celebrates-mass-before-huge-crowd/a-79442864?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The pope addressed around 700,000 people during a Mass at the Place de la Concorde, near the Champs-Elysees. Leo XIV is on a four-day visit to France.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia expected to intensify hybrid war on Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f7196defa369cc3666acaa5f08a06eac4555408a0d1ed6564232c0a98f8d977</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:06:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T15:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-expected-to-intensify-hybrid-war-on-europe/a-79444596--b27c55cf76ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-expected-to-intensify-hybrid-war-on-europe/a-79444596?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Drone explosions, airspace violations, arson attacks: Poland, Romania, and Moldova are now regularly targeted in Russian attacks against Ukraine. More governments are calling these attacks deliberate acts of aggression.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's FM Wadephul meets Lavrov on UNGA sidelines</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:690c4ee7aeac6543fda1e279a792f8fd5acaaaa9f6155b1d78fa581e511c2ab1</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:06:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-fm-wadephul-meets-lavrov-on-unga-sidelines/live-79366211--0b50744a8e02.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-fm-wadephul-meets-lavrov-on-unga-sidelines/live-79366211?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It's the first such meeting since Russia launched the invasion of Ukraine in February 2022. DW has the latest on day 5 of the UN General Assembly debate.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan: Suicide attack at police stop kills at least 11</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0b31220f14af0763ade356f27ee398dbde9d875076dd6db05f9e3a724d21096</id><updated>2026-09-27T14:06:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-suicide-attack-at-police-stop-kills-at-least-11/a-79443050--24fa32f41a80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-suicide-attack-at-police-stop-kills-at-least-11/a-79443050?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The blast was claimed by the Pakistani Taliban, which has stepped up attacks on Pakistani security forces in recent years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
